---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import Navbar from '../components/Navbar.astro';
import Scoreboard from '../components/Scoreboard.astro';
import GameBoard from '../components/GameBoard.astro';
import GameControls from '../components/GameControls.astro';
import VictoryModal from '../components/VictoryModal.astro';
import TutorialModal from '../components/TutorialModal.astro';
import StatsModal from '../components/StatsModal.astro';
import PlayerNamesModal from '../components/PlayerNamesModal.astro';
---

<Layout
	title="Dots and Boxes Game Online - Play Free 2 Player Strategy Game"
	description="Play the classic dots and boxes game online for free! Enjoy 2-player mode, challenge AI opponents, customize grid sizes, track stats, and learn winning strategies. No download required - play instantly in your browser."
	url="https://dotsandboxesgame.com"
>
	<main class="game-layout">
		<Navbar />
		<Scoreboard />
		<GameBoard />
		<GameControls />

		<!-- SEO Content Section -->
		<section class="seo-content" aria-labelledby="game-description">
			<div class="content-container">
				<h1 id="game-description" class="page-title">Dots and Boxes Game - Play Free Online</h1>
				
				<div class="game-intro">
					<p>Welcome to the ultimate <strong>dots and boxes game</strong> experience! Play the classic pencil-and-paper strategy game right in your browser - no downloads, no installations, just pure strategic fun. Whether you're looking to challenge a friend in <strong>dots and boxes 2 player</strong> mode, test your skills against our intelligent AI, or learn <strong>how to play dots and boxes</strong> from scratch, you've come to the right place.</p>
					
					<p>Our free online version brings this timeless game to life with modern features: customizable <strong>dots and boxes game board</strong> sizes, multiple difficulty levels, comprehensive statistics tracking, and smooth animations that make every completed box feel satisfying.</p>
				</div>

				<h2 class="section-heading">How to Play Dots and Boxes</h2>
				<div class="content-section">
					<p>Learning <strong>how to play dots and boxes</strong> is simple, but mastering it takes strategy and foresight. The game starts with an empty grid of dots. Players take turns drawing a single horizontal or vertical line between two adjacent dots. When a player completes the fourth side of a 1x1 box, they claim that box and get another turn.</p>
					
					<h3 class="subsection-heading">Basic Rules</h3>
					<ul class="rule-list">
						<li><strong>Setup:</strong> Choose your grid size (3x3, 4x4, 5x5, or larger)</li>
						<li><strong>Turns:</strong> Players alternate drawing one line per turn</li>
						<li><strong>Scoring:</strong> Complete a box to earn a point and take another turn</li>
						<li><strong>Winning:</strong> The player with the most boxes when the grid is full wins</li>
					</ul>
					
					<p>The beauty of this <strong>dots and boxes game</strong> lies in its simplicity - easy to learn in minutes, but offering deep strategic complexity that keeps players engaged for hours.</p>
				</div>

				<h2 class="section-heading">How to Win at Dots and Boxes - Pro Strategies</h2>
				<div class="content-section">
					<p>Understanding <strong>how to win dots and boxes</strong> requires more than just knowing the rules. Here are expert strategies to dominate every match:</p>
					
					<h3 class="subsection-heading">1. Avoid Creating Chains Early</h3>
					<p>The most critical concept in dots and boxes strategy is chain management. A "chain" is a sequence of boxes where each box shares a side with the next. Never be the first to give your opponent a chain of three or more boxes unless forced.</p>
					
					<h3 class="subsection-heading">2. The Double-Cross Strategy</h3>
					<p>When faced with a long chain, leave the last two boxes for your opponent. This forces them to open the next chain, giving you control of the game. This technique, known as the "double-cross," is the hallmark of advanced play.</p>
					
					<h3 class="subsection-heading">3. Control the Center</h3>
					<p>On larger <strong>dots and boxes game board</strong> configurations, controlling the center gives you more flexibility and forces your opponent to play on the edges where chains form more easily.</p>
					
					<h3 class="subsection-heading">4. Count Remaining Boxes</h3>
					<p>Always know how many boxes remain and who's ahead. In the endgame, precise counting lets you calculate whether to take a chain or sacrifice boxes to maintain control.</p>
				</div>

				<h2 class="section-heading">Game Modes & Features</h2>
				<div class="content-section">
					<h3 class="subsection-heading">2 Player Local Mode</h3>
					<p>Challenge a friend or family member in classic <strong>dots and boxes 2 player</strong> mode. Pass the device back and forth, or play side-by-side on the same screen. Perfect for game nights, classroom activities, or friendly competition.</p>
					
					<h3 class="subsection-heading">AI Opponents with Multiple Difficulties</h3>
					<p>No partner? No problem! Our AI engine offers three difficulty levels:
						<ul class="feature-list">
							<li><strong>Easy:</strong> Perfect for beginners learning the ropes</li>
							<li><strong>Medium:</strong> Uses basic chain avoidance strategies</li>
							<li><strong>Hard:</strong> Implements advanced double-cross tactics</li>
						</ul>
					</p>
					
					<h3 class="subsection-heading">Customizable Grid Sizes</h3>
					<p>From quick 3x3 games to epic 8x8 battles, adjust the <strong>dots and boxes game board</strong> to match your available time and desired challenge level. Smaller grids for fast games, larger grids for deep strategic battles.</p>
					
					<h3 class="subsection-heading">Statistics & Progress Tracking</h3>
					<p>Track your improvement with detailed stats: win rate, average game length, longest winning streak, boxes captured per game, and more. Watch your skills grow over time!</p>
				</div>

				<h2 class="section-heading">Dots and Boxes Printable Sheets</h2>
				<div class="content-section">
					<p>Prefer the traditional pen-and-paper experience? We've got you covered with free <strong>dots and boxes printable</strong> game sheets. Download and print grids in various sizes for offline play - perfect for classrooms, road trips, or screen-free family time.</p>
					
					<p>Our printable collection includes:</p>
					<ul class="feature-list">
						<li>Standard 3x3, 4x4, 5x5, and 6x6 grids</li>
						<li>Large-print versions for younger players</li>
						<li>Tournament-style score sheets</li>
						<li>Blank templates for custom sizes</li>
					</ul>
					
					<p>Simply download, print, and start playing - no internet connection required!</p>
				</div>

				<h2 class="section-heading">Why Play Dots and Boxes Online?</h2>
				<div class="content-section">
					<ul class="benefit-list">
						<li><strong>Instant Access:</strong> Play <strong>dots and boxes online</strong> anytime, anywhere - no app store visits needed</li>
						<li><strong>Cross-Platform:</strong> Works perfectly on desktop, tablet, and mobile browsers</li>
						<li><strong>Smart AI:</strong> Our adaptive AI provides a genuine challenge at every skill level</li>
						<li><strong>Zero Ads:</strong> Completely free with no interruptions or paywalls</li>
						<li><strong>Privacy-First:</strong> No accounts, no tracking, no personal data collected</li>
						<li><strong>Educational Value:</strong> Develops critical thinking, spatial reasoning, and strategic planning</li>
					</ul>
				</div>

				<h2 class="section-heading">History of Dots and Boxes</h2>
				<div class="content-section">
					<p>The <strong>dots and boxes game</strong> (also known as "Boxes," "Squares," "Paddocks," or "The Dot Game") was first published in 1889 by French mathematician Édouard Lucas. Originally a mathematical recreation, it quickly became a popular pastime worldwide.</p>
					
					<p>The game has been studied extensively in combinatorial game theory. Notably, Elwyn Berlekamp's book "The Dots and Boxes Game: Sophisticated Child's Play" revealed deep mathematical structures underlying the seemingly simple gameplay. Today, it remains a beloved classic that bridges casual entertainment and serious mathematical strategy.</p>
				</div>

				<h2 class="section-heading">Tips for Beginners</h2>
				<div class="content-section">
					<p>New to the game? Start here:</p>
					<ul class="tip-list">
						<li>Begin with a 3x3 or 4x4 grid to learn fundamentals</li>
						<li>Play against Easy AI until you consistently win</li>
						<li>Focus on not giving away 3-box chains</li>
						<li>Use the tutorial mode (accessible from the menu) for guided practice</li>
						<li>Watch your stats to identify patterns in your play</li>
					</ul>
				</div>

				<div class="cta-section">
					<p>Ready to play? The game is loaded above - just start drawing lines and claiming boxes! Challenge the AI, invite a friend for <strong>dots and boxes 2 player</strong> action, or explore different grid sizes to find your perfect match.</p>
				</div>
			</div>
		</section>
	</main>

	<!-- Modals -->
	<VictoryModal />
	<TutorialModal />
	<StatsModal />
	<PlayerNamesModal />
</Layout>

<script>
	import { initApp } from '../scripts/appController';

	document.addEventListener('DOMContentLoaded', () => {
		initApp();
	});
</script>

<style>
	.game-layout {
		width: 100%;
		min-height: 100vh;
		display: flex;
		flex-direction: column;
		align-items: center;
		justify-content: flex-start;
		padding-bottom: 60px;
	}
	
	.seo-content {
		width: 100%;
		max-width: 900px;
		padding: 3.5rem 1.5rem 2rem 1.5rem;
		margin-top: 2rem;
		position: relative;
	}

	.seo-content::before {
		content: "";
		position: absolute;
		top: 0;
		left: 50%;
		transform: translateX(-50%);
		width: 80%;
		max-width: 600px;
		height: 1px;
		background: linear-gradient(90deg, transparent, rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.1), rgba(56, 189, 248, 0.4), rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.1), transparent);
	}
	
	.content-container {
		display: flex;
		flex-direction: column;
		gap: 2.5rem;
	}
	
	.page-title {
		font-size: 2.25rem;
		font-weight: 800;
		line-height: 1.25;
		letter-spacing: -0.03em;
		color: #ffffff;
		margin-bottom: 0.5rem;
		text-align: center;
	}
	
	.game-intro {
		font-size: 1.05rem;
		line-height: 1.75;
		color: #cbd5e1;
	}
	
	.game-intro p {
		margin-bottom: 1.25rem;
	}

	.game-intro strong,
	.content-section strong {
		color: #ffffff;
		font-weight: 700;
	}
	
	.section-heading {
		font-size: 1.6rem;
		font-weight: 700;
		line-height: 1.35;
		letter-spacing: -0.02em;
		color: #ffffff;
		margin-bottom: 1rem;
		padding-bottom: 0.6rem;
		border-bottom: 1px solid rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.1);
	}
	
	.subsection-heading {
		font-size: 1.2rem;
		font-weight: 600;
		line-height: 1.4;
		color: #f1f5f9;
		margin: 1.5rem 0 0.75rem 0;
	}
	
	.content-section {
		font-size: 0.975rem;
		line-height: 1.75;
		color: #cbd5e1;
	}
	
	.content-section p {
		margin-bottom: 1rem;
	}
	
	.content-section ul {
		margin: 1rem 0 1rem 1.5rem;
	}
	
	.content-section li {
		margin-bottom: 0.5rem;
		line-height: 1.65;
		color: #cbd5e1;
	}
	
	.rule-list {
		list-style-type: disc;
	}
	
	.feature-list {
		list-style-type: disc;
	}
	
	.benefit-list {
		list-style-type: none;
		padding-left: 0;
	}
	
	.benefit-list li {
		position: relative;
		padding-left: 1.75rem;
		margin-bottom: 0.75rem;
	}
	
	.benefit-list li::before {
		content: "✓";
		position: absolute;
		left: 0;
		color: var(--player1-color);
		font-weight: 700;
	}
	
	.tip-list {
		list-style-type: decimal;
		margin-left: 1.5rem;
	}

	.tip-list li {
		color: #cbd5e1;
	}
	
	.cta-section {
		text-align: center;
		padding: 1.75rem;
		background: rgba(30, 41, 59, 0.7);
		backdrop-filter: blur(12px);
		-webkit-backdrop-filter: blur(12px);
		border: 1px solid var(--border-color);
		border-radius: var(--radius-md);
		margin-top: 1rem;
		box-shadow: var(--shadow-sm);
	}
	
	.cta-section p {
		font-size: 1.05rem;
		font-weight: 500;
		color: #f8fafc;
		margin: 0;
		line-height: 1.6;
	}

	.cta-section strong {
		color: var(--player1-color);
		font-weight: 700;
	}
	
	@media (max-width: 640px) {
		.page-title {
			font-size: 1.75rem;
		}
		
		.section-heading {
			font-size: 1.35rem;
		}
		
		.subsection-heading {
			font-size: 1.1rem;
		}
		
		.seo-content {
			padding: 2rem 1rem;
			margin-top: 1.5rem;
		}

		.game-intro,
		.content-section {
			font-size: 0.925rem;
		}
	}
</style>
